fix(ci): skip the pixel gate when no baseline is committed

CI has been red on every push since 1195656 enabled the gate. I misread this
as dormant in the previous commit's docs -- it was not.
`toHaveScreenshot` treats a missing snapshot as a failure: it writes the
actual and reports "A snapshot doesn't exist at ...". Turning the gate on
before any baseline existed therefore failed `day-ne`, `low-angle` and
`night-lanterns` on every run, rather than doing nothing.

The spec now resolves the expected path with `testInfo.snapshotPath()` and
asserts only when that file exists. Otherwise it records a
`pixel-gate-skipped` annotation naming the missing file, so the gap stays
visible in the report without failing the build. Committing the PNGs is all
it takes to arm the comparison -- no further code change.

`webgl-baselines` needs the opposite behaviour to bootstrap, so it sets
`LUXISO_WRITE_BASELINES=1` to force the assertion and let update mode mint
the snapshots.

Verified by reproducing CI locally. With `CI=1` and no baselines: 3 failures
before the change, 11/11 after. With `CI=1 LUXISO_WRITE_BASELINES=1` and
`--update-snapshots`: the three PNGs are written and the run passes, which is
also why the workflow step needs no `continue-on-error`. The locally
generated PNGs were deleted rather than committed -- they are win32 captures
and the gate expects Linux ones.

README, ACCEPTANCE and FRAMEWORK_ANALYSIS updated to describe the skip
mechanism, including a correction of the "wired but dormant" claim I made one
commit ago.
